
[38;5;231m⏺[39m [1mSection 3 — Testing and tooling[0m

  The repo has no test runner, no linter, no formatter, and no dependencies. Since this work creates the first module
  meant to be reused, it's the natural moment to decide how much of that to set up — it's cheapest now, before there are
  several forms depending on untested shared code.

  What the layering buys here: the rule factories and [38;5;153mvalidate()[39m are pure functions, so they test with zero
  infrastructure — [38;5;153mnode:test[39m and [38;5;153mnode:assert[39m ship with Node, and [38;5;153mnode --test[39m needs no dependency at all. That covers
  every rule, the first-failure-wins ordering, and the whitespace-only case.

  The DOM layer is the part that needs a decision. Testing [38;5;153mshowErrors[39m / [38;5;153mclearErrors[39m / [38;5;153mvalidateForm[39m means a DOM, which
  means either a [38;5;153mjsdom[39m devDependency — the first dependency this repo would ever take — or verifying that layer by hand
  in a browser. The find-or-create logic and the ARIA wiring are exactly the kind of thing that breaks quietly, so I
  lean toward covering it, but it's your call on the dependency.

  I'll write the tests first and let them drive the implementation either way.

